From 595ace6365bc00c69863067e5a8fbd83fdb41758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cgscli <cgscli@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:42:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] P7: CGS channels bill in the API relay's currency

Reason: CGS channels are billed by the API relay, in whatever currency the relay's console shows (yuan, dollars, or a custom symbol such as an emoji), not in dollars. The cgs extension reads that currency from the relay and exports the amount prefix in CGS_CURRENCY_PREFIX; omp prints it for cgs-* models in the model picker price column and the status line spend, and a new usage unit `currency` shows the relay wallet in it on /usage. omp's global stats (the stats database) record no cost for cgs-* (the relay has its own bill). The login and its four channels are shown as one provider name, Cicori Good Service. Every branch is new; other providers are unchanged.
Upstream: none yet (CGS-specific provider prefix, not a candidate PR)
Remove-when: the build no longer ships the cgs extension, or upstream supports per-provider currency, display names and externally billed providers
